<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss June car registrations fall 3.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Swiss June car registrations fall 3.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car registrations in Switzerland and Liechtenstein fell 3.1 percent in June from a year earlier to 26,601 vehicles.</p>
<p>There was a cumulative 4.2 percent decline to 149,596 in the first five months of the year, the Swiss Automobile Importers Association said. Leading exporters:</p>
<p>				     June 1997	June 1996</p>
<p>    Germany			 12,282	   12,697</p>
<p>    France			   3,829	    4,080</p>
<p>    Italy			    1,786	    2,413</p>
<p>    Japan			    5,616	    5,111</p>
<p>    Sweden			     815		850</p>
<p>    Britain			    442		419</p>
<p>    Korea				517		419</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
